    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "provides a simple test for epistasis. In the absence of epistasis, the expected value of $ \\Delta $ is zero because at every locus, by the Hardy-Weinberg law, the $ F_{2} $ is 25% $ P_{1}P_{1} $, 50% $ P_{1}P_{2} $, and 25% $ P_{2}P_{2} $. The sampling variance of this test statistic is",
      "source_page": 231,
      "printed_page": 211,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter9:p011:b10"
      ],
      "bbox": [
