      "content_sha256": "21094b68020298917c8e26a92d95580492fa050af7e90a1640b4ba3bd419eed1"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Under the reasonable assumption that the sampling distribution of $ \\Delta $ is approximately normal, the ratio $ |\\Delta|/\\sqrt{\\mathrm{Var}(\\Delta)} $ provides a simple $ t $ test for epistasis. For large samples, if this ratio is greater than 1.96, then the null hypothesis of no epistasis can be rejected with 95% confidence.",
      "source_page": 231,
      "printed_page": 211,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter9:p011:b13"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        44.0,
