    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the covariance matrix V for the residuals is diagonal with diagonal elements equal to the squared standard errors of the means. The treatment of V as a diagonal matrix assumes that the measured individuals from the different lines are unrelated, i.e., that there is no sampling covariance between the observed means.",
      "source_page": 232,
      "printed_page": 212,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter9:p012:b11"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        144.0,
