      "content_sha256": "51792132f0022b56e06bba410957b54f7b0d6d9a683d3905f51996feefa3477a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $k$ is the number of observed lines, provides a test statistic for the adequacy of the model (Appendix 3). Under the null hypothesis of purely additive gene action, this test statistic will be $\\chi^{2}$ distributed with degrees of freedom equal to the number of lines minus the number of estimated parameters, giving $(k-2)$ df.",
      "source_page": 233,
      "printed_page": 213,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter9:p013:b2"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        67.0,
        115.0,
        1027.0,
